  "correct": "2",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(4, 14, 828)\n\n(3, 10, 620)\n\n**Logic:** Third no. = [{(First no. × 100) + Second no.} × 2]\n\n**(4, 14, 828) →**\n\n⇒ [{(4 × 100) + 14} × 2]\n\n⇒ [(400 + 14) × 2]\n\n⇒ (414 × 2) = 828\n\n**(3, 10, 620) →**\n\n⇒ [{(3 × 100) + 10} × 2]\n\n⇒ [(300 + 10) × 2]\n\n⇒ (310 × 2) = 620\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1.** (1, 10, 100)\n\n⇒ [{(1 × 100) + 10} × 2]\n\n⇒ [(100 + 10) × 2]\n\n⇒ (110 × 2) = 220\n\n**2. (2, 50, 500)**\n\n⇒ [{(2 × 100) + 50} × 2]\n\n⇒ [(200 + 50) × 2]\n\n⇒ (250 × 2) = **500**\n\n**3.** (5, 10, 980)\n\n⇒ [{(5 × 100) + 10} × 2]\n\n⇒ [(500 + 10) × 2]\n\n⇒ (510 × 2) = 1020\n\n**4. **(4, 32, 98)\n\n⇒ [{(4 × 100) + 32} × 2]\n\n⇒ [(400 + 32) × 2]\n\n⇒ (432 × 2) = 864\n\nHere, **(2, 50, 500)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (2)\".",
